  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Generally tranquil weather is expected to prevail \nthrough at least the beginning of next week. \n\nHigh pressure continues to shift offshore through the rest of today \nand tonight as low pressure moves through eastern Canada. A dry cold \nfront associated with this low will move through tomorrow morning. \nHigh pressure will then return through early next week with \ncontinuing mild and dry conditions expected.\n\nAfter a relatively warm day today, it will be mild tonight with lows \nin the upper 40s to low 50s. Friday will turn breezy in the wake of \nthe morning cold frontal passage. Northwest winds 10-15 mph with \ngusts up to 25 mph can be expected.\n\nConditions will turn cooler again for the weekend. Lows Friday night \nthrough Sunday night will be mainly in the mid 30s to mid 40s, but \nfrost currently appears unlikely where the growing season continues. \nHighs will be coolest on Halloween, in the upper 50s to low 60s, \nunder partly cloudy skies. Partly to mostly cloudy skies Sunday, but \na bit milder with highs in the low to mid 60s. \n\nThe system which had potential to affect the region early next week \nnow appears to weaken and miss our region for the most part. This \nwill keep our region dry, but still increase cloud cover. We cannot \ntotally rule out a few showers midweek, but the next period to keep \nan eye on for widespread rainfall looks to be toward the end of next \nweek (Thursday into Friday), when guidance suggests a more prolific \nsystem may impact the region.",
